title TACT-J2r1 — the offline-verifiable publication receipt
prompt continue the road Lindy-first crux-first; keep agent-doable work moving; send each increment; stop at custody gates
think Journey 1 (Ship-Pilot) complete end to end. Opened Journey 2 (Publishing) with a self-approved design round. Its crux is the detached, portable receipt a recipient verifies offline; the serve rung reaching the Comlink-served custody gate is r4 (Keaton's hand).
think r1 carries BUHR-J7r4's signed word out of the store into a Publication receipt (point, name, whole_len, digest, sig). Verification is offline in two honest halves: the signature over the bound facts by the keeper key (no content needed), and — when content is held — the SHA-256 matching the bound digest.
think Exposed two additive pub functions in tablecloth_keyed.rye (BUHR-J7r4): digest_of (the content digest) and verify_receipt (verify from the bound digest, no content, no store) — reusing the exact auth_message layout so a detached receipt and a stored publication carry the identical signed word. The BUHR keyed witness re-runs GREEN.
think Five cases proven: a real receipt verifies offline + content matches; a forged signature refuses; a wrong keeper key refuses (names exactly who published); an authentic receipt still refuses swapped content (the digest is bound in); an overlong name refuses NameTooLong rather than truncate the signed word.
obs One shadow fix: the witness helper keeper_pubkey shadowed the verify_offline parameter of the same name → renamed the helper pubkey_of.
obs Demo keeper seeds only, signing/verifying in-process, no store handle, no network. The serve transport stays the Comlink-served custody gate.
loom witness=tact_publish_receipt_witness result=GREEN cases=5 halves=2
file pond/apps/publish_receipt.rye the detached publication receipt; offline two-half verify, forgery/wrong-key/tamper refused
file pond/apps/tablecloth_keyed.rye additive pub digest_of + verify_receipt (offline verify from the bound digest); BUHR witness re-runs GREEN
file tools/tact_publish_receipt_witness.rish witness — GREEN (5 cases + keyed re-run)
